.Dd September 28, 2026
.Dt UUIDGEN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm uuidgen
.Nd generate a universally unique identifier
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hdr
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility generates a new universally unique identifier (UUID) and writes it
to standard output as a 36-character string of hexadecimal digits separated
by hyphens, in the canonical 8-4-4-4-12 form
.Pq e.g. Ns Pa 67B63244-8A03-4B4C-BE96-3F1B4E5A9C10 Ns and Dd Ns Ar upper-case
hexadecimal.
.Pp
The identifier is drawn from a version 4 (pseudo-random) source by
default.
The only option accepted is
.Fl hdr ,
which emits the result in a form suitable for pasting into a C header
instead of as a bare identifier.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl hdr
Emit the result as a C declaration rather than as a bare identifier.
Three lines are written: a
.Pp
.Dl // Ar uuid
.Dl
comment naming the identifier, a
.Dl #warning Change the macro name MYUUID below to something useful!
.Dl
directive, and a
.Pp
.Dl #define MYUUID CFUUIDGetConstantUUIDWithBytes(kCFAllocatorSystemDefault, ... )
.Dl
macro expanding to the sixteen constituent bytes of the identifier.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CFUUIDVersionNumber
If this variable is set and its value parses as the number
.Ql 1 ,
.Nm
generates a version 1 (time-based) identifier instead of a version 4
identifier.
Any other value, including a value that does not parse as a number, is
ignored and leaves the generator at version 4.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
An unrecognized option, or more than one argument, prints the usage summary
to standard error and exits with a status of 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print an identifier:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ uuidgen
67B63244-8A03-4B4C-BE96-3F1B4E5A9C10
.Ed
.Pp
Produce a header-ready declaration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ uuidgen -hdr
// 67B63244-8A03-4B4C-BE96-3F1B4E5A9C10
#warning Change the macro name MYUUID below to something useful!
#define MYUUID CFUUIDGetConstantUUIDWithBytes(kCFAllocatorSystemDefault, 0x67, 0xB6, \
0x32, 0x44, 0x8A, 0x03, 0x4B, 0x4C, 0xBE, 0x96, 0x3F, 0x1B, 0x4E, 0x5A, 0x9C, 0x10)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uuid 3 ,
.Xr uuid_string 3
.Sh HISTORY
This implementation is a clean-room rewrite of the CoreFoundation
.Nm
utility, which is distributed in the base system but is not part of
Apple's published CoreFoundation source release.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An LibreDarwin
